# AI Usage Log

**Tools Used**

ChatGPT (OpenAI)

During this assignment, I used ChatGPT as a learning and development assistant while building BIDCAMP, an auction platform using HTML, Tailwind CSS, JavaScript, Vite, and the Noroff Auction API v2.

I mainly used ChatGPT to explore implementation approaches, understand technical concepts, troubleshoot issues, and improve the structure and maintainability of my application.

ChatGPT also provided code examples and draft implementations for parts of the project. I worked with these suggestions during development, tested the results, and compared the implementation with my Figma designs and the assignment requirements.

## Areas Where I Used AI

**Purpose:**

- Understanding the assignment requirements and planning the application structure.
- Configuring Vite and Tailwind CSS.
- Exploring approaches to JavaScript functionality, DOM manipulation, and API integration.
- Understanding authentication and working with the Noroff Auction API v2.
- Receiving implementation suggestions and code examples for different features.
- Working with responsive layouts and mobile-first development.
- Improving code organization through DRY and Separation of Concerns.
- Troubleshooting errors and reviewing possible improvements.

**Outcome:**

- I developed the BIDCAMP design in Figma and used it as the main reference throughout development.
- I set up the development environment using Vite and Tailwind CSS.
- I worked with AI-assisted suggestions when implementing authentication, navigation, auction listings, and profile functionality.
- I integrated functionality using the Noroff Auction API v2.
- I used reusable JavaScript components and CSS classes to keep the application consistent.
- I organized the code into separate files for API requests, pages, components, and styling.
- I identified and resolved issues related to routing, imports, API data, and responsive layouts with debugging assistance.
- I tested the application in the browser and made adjustments based on functionality, design consistency, and usability.

**Reflection**

Using ChatGPT helped me strengthen my understanding of JavaScript, API integration, and responsive development with Tailwind CSS.

I became more aware of the importance of reusable components, DRY, and Separation of Concerns when building a larger application.

AI was particularly useful for exploring solutions and troubleshooting problems during development. I also found it important to evaluate suggestions against the Noroff documentation and my own design requirements rather than treating every suggestion as the final solution.

Overall, ChatGPT has been a useful supporting tool in my development process, helping me explore different approaches and improve the organization and functionality of BIDCAMP.
